# Isotactic polypropylene, α (α2, ordered): M. Hikosaka & T. Seto, Polym. J. 5, 111 (1973), doi:10.1295/polymj.5.111
# space group P21/c (b unique, c the chain axis) (No. 14), Z = 12 C3H6 per cell; cells p. 112 (specimen B: a 6.65, b 20.73, c 6.50 A, beta 98 deg 40 min); Table Ia p. 115 (carbon only)
# correction / model: the appendix's equivalent positions (pp. 126-127) do not fit Table Ia; the standard P21/c positions (x,y,z; -x,1/2+y,1/2-z; -x,-y,-z; x,1/2-y,1/2+z) do: every C-C 1.54 A and the paper's structure factors of Table Ib are reproduced
# correction / model: the ordered limiting structure alpha2 (all chains up/down as in P21/c); the alpha1 form is the statistical C2/c up/down model of the same coordinates
# hydrogens: none in the paper; placed by tools/make_polymer_crystals.py (CH, CH2, CH3; C-H 1.09 A sp3, 1.08 A sp2, N-H 1.01 A, tetrahedral / in-plane angles)
# written in P1 with every atom of the paper's cell; 0.9466 g/cm3, shortest contacts beyond 1-3: H...H 1.99 A, H...X 2.62 A, X...X 3.01 A
